= The Debt Ceiling Standoff

Republicans in the House are threatening default unless we accept deep spending cuts. Markets are nervous; time is running out.

- @debt_negotiate: Negotiate a deal
- @debt_stand: Refuse to negotiate over the debt limit

@debt_negotiate
on-arrival: budget += 2; economic_growth -= 0.2; progressive_dissent += 5; gopmod_relation += 3; institutions += 1

A deal averts default, with cuts we dislike.

@debt_stand
on-arrival: polarization += 2; biz_relation -= 3; institutions += 0; economic_growth -= 0.8; progressive_dissent -= 2; moderate_dissent += 3

We refuse. The brinkmanship is terrifying, and the outcome is uncertain.
